  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/esa-notional-income
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: Deprivation is expressly one possible basis for notional income; it is not a synonym for all notional-income cases.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol9-ch51/0127
      quote: "51457 Notional income may be calculated because of\n\n\n1. deprivation of income\n\n\n2. income available if applied for (including special rules for personal pensions)\n\n\n3. income due but not yet paid\n\n\n4. income for a member of the family paid to a third party\n\n\n5. income for a third party made to a member of the family.\n\n\n\nActual and notional income"
      locator: DMG 51457
  - target: term/dmg-evidence-assessment
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source lists explanations, timing, knowledge and the likelihood of a claim as relevant facts when assessing benefit purpose.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol9-ch51/0132
      quote: "51486 It is unlikely that there will be direct evidence that a deprivation was for the purpose of getting\nbenefit. Decide on a person's reasons for disposing of an income after considering all the facts of the\ncase. These may include\n\n\n1. the person's explanations\n\n\n2. the timing of the disposal\n\n\n3. the claimant's knowledge of the benefit system\n\n\n4. the likelihood of a benefit claim at the time of the deprivation."
      locator: DMG 51486
